steps.text:
Threat-model the planned work before it is built. The card: {{title}}.

{{brief}}

Read the plan at the absolute path `{{planPath}}`; if it does not exist yet, work from the brief and the repository as it stands. Walk the change's new surface: inputs, outputs, trust boundaries, stored data, and what becomes reachable that was not before. For each, ask the quick questions — can it be spoofed, tampered with, repurposed, disclosed, repudiated, or elevated? Write the model to the absolute path `{{reportPath}}`: a table of threats (threat, entry point, who, worst credible outcome, what the plan already does, what test would prove it handled), then a short list titled "The plan must name" — the tests or decisions still missing. Severity honestly: most threats are low, and inflating them erodes the alarm. Fail the stage only for a critical threat that is both plausible and completely unaddressed by the plan; pass otherwise, with the must-name list as your payload. If the change adds no new surface (a refactor, a copy edit), say exactly that and pass.
